## Lore

The Kwarla are the Koala people of the forests: short, about four feet
tall, but enormously heavy, with thick muscle under short grey, silver or
reddish-brown fur, large swept-back ears, a black nose and a set of black
claws that do not retract. Aboriginal lore says the Koala spirit took a
human tribe at the Coming of the Rifts, gave it his strength and wisdom,
and handed over all his anger as well so that he could go on dozing in his
tree. Since then they have spread through the humid and forested parts of
the country, from Queensland down the east coast to Victoria and west into
the Northland.

They are peaceful, tribal tree-dwellers who live in mud-and-stick huts
fixed to the tallest trees, and they are nature''s guardians: their hatred
of supernatural evil and of anything wantonly destructive runs deep. Their
tools and weapons are wood, bone and tooth, often timber from a Millennium
Tree, which they hold as a great ally. Machines they have seen and count as
one more kind of demon.

A Kwarla is blunt and literal; lying and guile are foreign to it. It makes
a solid, dependable friend to anyone who earns its respect with courage,
and it values the tribe and the team above single combat. Kwarla are also
masters of the ambush, dropping from the trees to pin an enemy under their
claws.

## GM Notes

The book prints one stat block for the whole race and three ways to play
it. Males are Demon Hunters or Mystics: pair this race with the Kwarla
Demon Hunter or Kwarla Mystic class. Females are Providers, the caretakers
and backbone of a tribe: choose the Provider variant, which adds its skill
list and the female''s +2D6 I.S.P.

Psionics by sex: a male rolls 1D4 and takes that many Physical powers; a
female rolls 1D4+1 and takes that many Sensitive or Healing powers. The
picker cannot roll, so it offers the maximum.

Horror Factor 8 (11 for three or more) applies only to evil supernatural
beings and evil sorcerers.

Size 3 feet plus 3D6 inches (0.9 to 1.37 m); weight 220 + 6D6 pounds of
muscle and fur; life span 60 + 2D6 years. Omnivores who prefer plants,
eucalyptus leaves above all, and rarely cook meat.

They get on well with other tribal people, with Bushmen and rugged
Jackaroos, and with heroes who fight the supernatural; they are at odds
with most others who are destructive toward nature. Habitat is heavy
forest, rainforest and thick bushland. Demons, Necromancers and other evil
beings wear their hides and skulls as trophies.

The block prints no starting equipment and no money.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kwarla');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kwarla';

